# Firebase Functions Environment Configuration
# 
# Set secrets using Firebase CLI (RECOMMENDED - Modern approach):
# firebase functions:secrets:set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
# Enter your sk_test_... or sk_live_... key when prompted
#
# Alternative: Set via Firebase Console:
# 1. Go to Firebase Console → Your Project → Functions → Secrets
# 2. Add Secret: STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
# 3. Value: Your Stripe secret key
#
# For local development, create a .env file in functions/ directory:
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_yourTestKeyHere
#
# Production Stripe Configuration:
# - Test Mode: sk_test_... (for development/staging)
# - Live Mode: sk_live_... (for production)
# - Replace 'price_123' in createCheckout function with your actual Stripe Price ID
#
# SECURITY NOTES:
# ✅ Never commit actual API keys to version control
# ✅ Use Firebase secrets for production
# ✅ Test with sk_test_ keys first
# ✅ Update CORS origins in functions for your domain